.TH NSSH 1 "August 2026" "nssh 0.23.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nssh \- SSH reverse tunnel client for NAT traversal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nssh
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIuser@server\fR
.br
.B nssh
\-R \fIremote_port\fR:\fIlocal_host\fR:\fIlocal_port\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIuser@server\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nssh
is a lightweight SSH reverse tunnel client written in Go. It exposes local
services behind NAT or firewalls to the public internet through a standard
OpenSSH server (sshd), speaking the SSH protocol natively without requiring a
dedicated server component.
.PP
It supports auto-reconnect with a configurable delay, heartbeat keep-alive,
password or SSH-key authentication, and a background daemon that manages
multiple tunnels.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-remote " " \fIremote_port\fR:\fIlocal_host\fR:\fIlocal_port\fR
Set up a reverse tunnel from \fIremote_port\fR on the server to
\fIlocal_host\fR:\fIlocal_port\fR on the client.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
SSH server port (default 20022).
.TP
.BR \-P ", " \-\-passwd " " \fIPASSWORD\fR
SSH password for authentication.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-identity " " \fIFILE\fR
SSH private key file for authentication.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reconnect " " \fISECONDS\fR
Reconnect delay after a disconnect (default 30).
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Run as a background daemon with automatic reconnect.
.TP
.B \-\-list
List all tunnels managed by the daemon.
.TP
.BR \-\-stop " " \fIuser\fR
Stop a tunnel managed by the daemon.
.TP
.B \-\-stop\-all
Stop all tunnels managed by the daemon.
.TP
.BR \-\-restart " " \fIuser\fR
Restart a tunnel managed by the daemon.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show version information.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Expose local port 80 to the public port 8080 on the server:
.PP
.RS
nssh \-R 8080:localhost:80 user@example.com \-p 2122 \-P password
.RE
